  "instructions": [
    "Pat the pork chops dry. Season both sides with the salt, pepper, and thyme.",
    "Heat the olive oil in a 12 inch skillet over medium-high heat until it shimmers.",
    "Sear the chops for 4 minutes per side until deep golden. Move them to a plate.",
    "Lower the heat to medium. Add the onion to the skillet and cook for 4 minutes, stirring, until soft.",
    "Add the apples and maple syrup. Cook for 3 minutes until the apples start to soften.",
    "Pour in the apple juice and vinegar. Scrape up the browned bits and simmer for 2 minutes.",
    "Return the chops and any juices to the skillet. Cook for 3 to 4 minutes, spooning the apples over the top, until the pork reads 145 F in the thickest part.",
    "Rest the chops for 3 minutes. Serve with the apples, onions, and pan sauce spooned over."
